    {
      "step": "every scenario's setup and every apply_doc that changes the rule set",
      "cause": "The account stores the rule-eval rules its installed rules enforce (PerchSmartAccount::rule_set), aligned with its installed-rule records, in one new persistent entry, key RuleSet. The constructor writes it with the admin rule, so each scenario's setup writes it; every accepted apply_doc whose lowered rule set differs from the stored one writes it again, and one that leaves it unchanged (a re-apply, a rejected document) writes nothing. Each of these steps' outcome, events, authorization failures and every other storage entry are unchanged, the entry's live_until included.",
